  "narrative": {
    "text": "'Sites of child vaccines': a photograph of a seated baby with labelled arrows. Polio, Vitamin A, Rota (Oral) to the mouth; BCG (Intradermal) and Yellow Fever (Subcutaneous) to the baby's right upper arm; Measles-Rubella (Subcutaneous) to the baby's left upper arm; IPV (2cm apart) (Intramuscular) and PCV (2cm apart) (Intramuscular) to the baby's right thigh; Hep B Birth dose (Intramuscular) and DPT-HepB-Hib (Intramuscular) to the baby's left thigh. Sides are read from the arrows: the baby faces the viewer.",
